{
  // The app/worker program. It does NOT compile server sources: the worker
  // entry's `typeof import("../server/index")` and the ~30 direct
  // `app/** -> server/**` imports used to drag ~800 server .ts files into this
  // program, which is what made a cold `type-check:app` exceed an 8 GB heap.
  //
  // The `references` entry below redirects every one of those imports to the
  // `.d.ts` that tsconfig.api.json already emits: measured with --listFiles,
  // this program now contains ZERO server .ts files and 328 declaration files.
  // Cold, at an 8 GB ceiling: 45s / 1,190,402 instantiations / 1.32 GB. The
  // same pass before the split OOM'd at that ceiling after 281s.
  //
  // Consequences worth knowing:
  //   - Both type-check entry points are `tsc -b`, not `tsc -p`. Build mode is
  //     what builds/refreshes the referenced project's `.d.ts`; `tsc -p` would
  //     just report that the outputs are missing.
  //   - `type-check:app` therefore performs an up-to-date check on the api
  //     project first. When nothing under server/ changed that is a stat pass;
  //     when something did, the rebuild is real work this program now depends on.
  //   - `.types/` is generated and gitignored. Never commit it.
  "references": [{ "path": "./tsconfig.api.json" }],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "strict": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    // ⚠️ THE LAST TWO ARE FOR THE CO-LOCATED SPECS, and each was measured
    // rather than assumed (each entry removed, program recompiled, errors
    // counted):
    //
    //   `vitest/globals` — vitest.config.ts sets `globals: true`, and 201 of
    //     the 352 specs use `describe`/`it`/`expect` without importing them.
    //     Same call `tsconfig.tests.json` already makes for the same reason.
    //   `@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest` — the SUBPATH, which is what carries
    //     the `Assertion` augmentation for `toBeChecked()`/`toBeDisabled()`/
    //     `toHaveTextContent()`. Without it: 19 x TS2339. It is loaded at
    //     runtime by `tests/setup-web.ts`, which is in the tests program, not
    //     this one — so the augmentation had no way in.
    //
    // `@types/node` is deliberately NOT here. Four specs read fixtures through
    // `node:fs`/`node:path`/`node:url`, which looks like it needs it — measured,
    // it does not: `worker-configuration.d.ts` is generated with
    // `nodejs_compat` and already declares those modules. Adding it anyway
    // would put `NodeJS.Timeout` into ~685 browser source files' `setTimeout`,
    // which is a loosening this program has no reason to buy.
    "types": [
      "vite/client",
      "@cloudflare/workers-types",
      "vitest/globals",
      "@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest"
    ],
    "paths": {
      "~/*": ["./app/*"],
      "@core/shared-ui": ["./packages/shared-ui/src/index.ts"]
    },
    "rootDirs": [".", "./.react-router/types"],
    "noEmit": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "incremental": true,
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./.tsbuildinfo.app"
  },
  "include": [
    ".react-router/types/**/*",
    "app/**/*.ts",
    "app/**/*.tsx",
    "workers/**/*.ts",
    "vite.config.ts",
    // The worker entry's `typeof import("../server/index")` pulls the server
    // graph into this program too, so server-side ambient declarations the
    // graph relies on must be visible here (they live under the api config's
    // server/** include).
    "server/types/qrcode-internals.d.ts",
    // Needed so the global `Env` type (declared here as `interface Env extends Cloudflare.Env {}`)
    // is visible when the worker entry re-exports DOs that use it (e.g. InspectorMcp
    // extends McpAgent<Env>). McpAgent constrains its Env param to `extends Cloudflare.Env`,
    // and only the global `Env` satisfies that after Cloudflare.Env is augmented by this file.
    "worker-configuration.d.ts",
    // packages/shared-ui SOURCES already reached this program transitively, via
    // the `@core/shared-ui` path alias every app route imports. Its 19
    // co-located specs did not — nothing imports a spec — so they belonged to no
    // program at all, the same hole `app/**/*.test.*` was in. Listing the tree
    // explicitly also brings in any component that no route happens to import
    // yet, which is the state a new one starts in.
    //
    // ⚠️ `packages/shared-ui/tsconfig.json` is an ORPHAN: no config references
    // it, no npm script runs it, no tool reads it. It is NOT what checks these
    // files, and editing it will not affect anything. This is.
    "packages/shared-ui/src/**/*.ts",
    "packages/shared-ui/src/**/*.tsx"
  ],
  // ⚠️ NO SPEC EXCLUSIONS, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING.
  //
  // `app/**/*.test.ts(x)` used to be excluded here, justified by "no vitest /
  // @testing-library types in this tsc program". That was true and fixable: the
  // two `types` entries added above are the whole fix. What the exclusion cost
  // was 333 co-located specs + 19 under packages/shared-ui compiled by ZERO tsc
  // programs — vitest strips types with esbuild and never checks them, and
  // eslint skips them for the matching reason (see the `ignores` note in
  // eslint.config.js, whose stated premise this change retires).
  //
  // Cost of taking them, measured COLD (build-info deleted, which is the only
  // honest way — pre-commit runs warm, CI always runs cold): the program goes
  // 2612 -> 3038 files and 1,203,400 -> 1,279,085 instantiations (+6.3%), and
  // the heap FLOOR does not move at all: 1024 MB OOMs and 1280 MB passes, both
  // before and after. Wall clock +4s.
  //
  // The alternative that was measured and rejected was a separate program
  // REFERENCING this one (the shape tsconfig.tests.json uses for api). It needs
  // this project to be `composite` and emit declarations, and declaration emit
  // over app/** does not come free: 30 x TS6307 (a composite project must list
  // every input, so packages/shared-ui had to be enumerated anyway) plus 3 x
  // TS2742 and 1 x TS4058 that can only be fixed by ANNOTATING app source — a
  // tax every future hook returning a react-router internal type would pay, in
  // exchange for saving 4 seconds.
  //
  // `scripts/check-tests-tsconfig.mjs` pins this array: an entry added here
  // that is not in `scripts/tests-tsconfig-baseline.json` fails the gate. That
  // list is EMPTY on purpose. Excluding a spec is not a fix, and the reason
  // this program exists is that "temporarily" excluded specs are how the last
  // 352 got here.
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "build", "dist"]
}
